   "h": "Generalized Edema scheme (Blackbook)",
   "html": "<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b108a\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "op": "append",
   "sec": "class-gen",
   "html": "<ul><li><b>Overfill</b> (increased renal sodium retention, urine Na &gt; 40 meq/L): NSAIDs, AKI/CKD, nephrotic syndrome</li><li><b>Underfill</b> (urine Na &lt; 20 meq/L): altered Starling forces (absolute decrease in EABV) or congestive heart failure “forward failure” (relative decrease in EABV; signs of left ventricular failure)</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "op": "append",
   "sec": "cause",
   "html": "<p>Altered Starling forces:</p><ul><li>Increased interstitial oncotic pressure: myxedema (hypothyroid)</li><li>Increased capillary hydrostatic pressure: right heart failure, constrictive pericarditis, portal hypertension, pregnancy</li><li>Decreased capillary oncotic pressure (low serum albumin due to loss or impaired synthesis): nephrotic syndrome, cirrhosis</li><li>Increased capillary permeability (severely ill, e.g. in ICU): inflammation, sepsis, acute respiratory distress syndrome, allergies, burns/trauma</li></ul>"
  }
 ],
